   "TrashedCells" -> {".md\nGraphical output"}|>, 
 "Cells" -> {<|"Data" -> ".md\n# Quantum Well\nSolving the time-independent \
Schr\[ODoubleDot]dinger equation for a **finite square quantum well** using \
numerical eigensystem methods. This notebook computes the first few \
bound-state energy levels and wavefunctions, and provides an interactive \
visualization to explore how they depend on the well depth, particle mass, \
and well half-width.", "Display" -> "codemirror", 
    "Hash" -> "1cef42bb-bb6f-4282-ada9-0054d128102e", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <|"Hidden" -> True|>, 
    "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", 
    "UID" -> Null, "Notebook" -> "3f753daa-f73d-4fc3-9ead-85a10dede7d0"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "# Quantum Well\nSolving the time-independent \
Schr\[ODoubleDot]dinger equation for a **finite square quantum well** using \
numerical eigensystem methods. This notebook computes the first few \
bound-state energy levels and wavefunctions, and provides an interactive \
visualization to explore how they depend on the well depth, particle mass, \
and well half-width.", "Display" -> "markdown", 
    "Hash" -> "5007a026-c5c1-4bb8-8ecc-80daae4c9ab4", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Output", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "3f753daa-f73d-4fc3-9ead-85a10dede7d0"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> ".md\n## Initial parameters\nClear all symbols to avoid \
conflicts. We use natural units where \[HBar] = 1 throughout.", 
    "Display" -> "codemirror", "Hash" -> 
     "3448160e-d607-41b1-8f03-e88b06346431", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <|"Hidden" -> True|>, 
    "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", 
    "UID" -> Null, "Notebook" -> "3f753daa-f73d-4fc3-9ead-85a10dede7d0"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "## Initial parameters\nClear all symbols to avoid conflicts. \
We use natural units where \[HBar] = 1 throughout.", "Display" -> "markdown", 
    "Hash" -> "52c509dc-5c33-49e0-81b0-c7ddd2a3bd75", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Output", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "3f753daa-f73d-4fc3-9ead-85a10dede7d0"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "ClearAll[v0, hb, d, m, V, op, u, V, x];", 
    "Display" -> "codemirror", "Hash" -> 
     "f63c838d-6505-469c-9664-fa63fe9092ea", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <|"InitGroup" -> True|>, 
    "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", 
    "UID" -> Null, "Notebook" -> "3f753daa-f73d-4fc3-9ead-85a10dede7d0"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> ".md\n## Potential and Hamiltonian operator\nDefine the finite \
square well potential `V(x)` \[LongDash] zero inside the well (|x| < d) and \
`v0` outside \[LongDash] and the 1D Hamiltonian operator \
`\[Minus](\[HBar]\262/2m) \[PartialD]\262/\[PartialD]x\262 + V(x)`.", 
    "Display" -> "codemirror", "Hash" -> 
     "bd74510b-b093-4c3c-a301-483a1a7406fb", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <|"Hidden" -> True|>, 
    "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", 
    "UID" -> Null, "Notebook" -> "3f753daa-f73d-4fc3-9ead-85a10dede7d0"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "## Potential and Hamiltonian operator\nDefine the finite \
square well potential `V(x)` \[LongDash] zero inside the well (|x| < d) and \
`v0` outside \[LongDash] and the 1D Hamiltonian operator \
`\[Minus](\[HBar]\262/2m) \[PartialD]\262/\[PartialD]x\262 + V(x)`.", 
    "Display" -> "markdown", "Hash" -> 
     "8458ddec-f8bd-428d-bb61-392605d98e73", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Output", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "3f753daa-f73d-4fc3-9ead-85a10dede7d0"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "V[x_, v0_, d_] := \
(*TB[*)Piecewise[{{(*|*)0(*|*),(*|*)-d<=x<d(*|*)},{(*|*)v0(*|*),(*|*)True(*|*\
)}}](*|*)(*1:eJxTTMoPSmNkYGAo5gESAZmpyanlmcWpTvkVmUxAAQBzVQdd*)(*]TB*) \
;\n\nop[u_[x_], m_, rest__] := - \
(*FB[*)(((*SpB[*)Power[hb(*|*),(*|*)2](*]SpB*))(*,*)/(*,*)(2 m))(*]FB*) \
u''[x] + V[x, rest] u[x];", "Display" -> "codemirror", 
    "Hash" -> "ec558b2b-6eae-4ebc-a328-b1c8aa6ff000", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <|"InitGroup" -> True|>, 
    "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", 
    "UID" -> Null, "Notebook" -> "3f753daa-f73d-4fc3-9ead-85a10dede7d0"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> ".md\n## Interactive eigenstate viewer\nUse `NDEigensystem` to \
numerically solve for the first 6 energy eigenvalues and eigenfunctions with \
Dirichlet boundary conditions. The wavefunctions are shifted vertically by \
their energy for easy visualization. The black line shows the potential \
profile. Adjust **V0** (well depth), **Mass**, and **d** (half-width) with \
the sliders.", "Display" -> "codemirror", 
    "Hash" -> "99f9a62c-48f0-4979-ab58-e3dcddf6b4d3", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <|"Hidden" -> True|>, 
    "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", 
    "UID" -> Null, "Notebook" -> "3f753daa-f73d-4fc3-9ead-85a10dede7d0"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "## Interactive eigenstate viewer\nUse `NDEigensystem` to \
numerically solve for the first 6 energy eigenvalues and eigenfunctions with \
Dirichlet boundary conditions. The wavefunctions are shifted vertically by \
their energy for easy visualization. The black line shows the potential \
profile. Adjust **V0** (well depth), **Mass**, and **d** (half-width) with \
the sliders.", "Display" -> "markdown", 
    "Hash" -> "ac8355bc-a254-4cbe-97fc-16307e6e734c", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Output", "UID" -> Null, 
    "Notebook" -> "3f753daa-f73d-4fc3-9ead-85a10dede7d0"|>, 
   <|"Data" -> "Manipulate[Block[{ev, ef, hb = 1.0},\n\n  {ev, ef} = \
NDEigensystem[{\n    op[u[x], m, v0, d], DirichletCondition[u[x] == 0, \
True]\n  }, u[x], {x, -2, 2}, 6];\n\n  Plot[Evaluate[ef + ev], {x,-2,2}, \
PlotRange->Full, Epilog->{\n    Line @ Table[{x, V[x, v0, d] 2}, \
{x,-2,2,0.1}]\n  }]\n], \n  {{v0, 7, \"V0\"}, 1,7,3},\n  {{m, 1.0, \"Mass\"}, \
1,5,1},\n  {{d, 0.1 3, \"d\"}, 0.1,0.1 5,0.1},\n  ContinuousAction->True\n]", 
    "Display" -> "codemirror", "Hash" -> 
     "ca3c6976-68cc-4f1d-aaf9-3683bafc4a8e", "Invisible" -> False, 
    "MetaOnly" -> False, "Props" -> <||>, "PublicFields" -> {"Properties"}, 
    "State" -> "Idle", "Type" -> "Input", "UID" -> Null, 
